<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nasiruddin Mahmud Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1435">1435</a>–1459</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Nasiruddin Mahmud Shah I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nasiruddin Mahmud Shah was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> from about 1435 to 1459, a descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shamsuddin-ilyas-shah">Shamsuddin Ilyas Shah</a> who restored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilyas-shahi-dynasty">Ilyas Shahi dynasty</a> after the end of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raja-ganesha">Raja Ganesha</a>'s line. His reign was peaceful; he rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaur">Gaur</a> as the capital and built mosques, bridges and fortifications there. His dynasty ruled until it was overthrown by Abyssinian palace guards in 1487.</p></div>
